Subject: [PATCH] Re-sync the two repository mirrors from validated sources

Cross-Domain-Contracts and User-Checklist are mirrors of files that live in
the repository, because tests and tooling read those from disk. Both wiki
copies were 2026-08-01 snapshots that had drifted badly - the contracts page
was 123 lines against the repository's 371, missing the entire post-refactor
reconciliation.

Both sources were re-verified file by file before this sync. The contracts
file in particular was substantially wrong and has been rewritten in the
repository: four of its nine contracts are now marked VOID or SUPERSEDED
because they coordinated Terraform modules that ADR 0013 deleted, and the
surviving contracts' file inventories were corrected against the real tree.
Contract numbers were deliberately NOT renumbered - they are cited by number
in live code and asserted in factory/tests/Test-Bootstrap.ps1.

Each page now carries a provenance header naming its source path, the commit
it was synced from, and the rule that the repository wins on any
disagreement.
